text:
jamal: Quick sync — seeing intermittent JSON.parse errors in our Node streaming client when token refresh (401) happens mid-stream. Payloads arriving as partial chunks, e.g. first chunk: `{"choices": [{"text": "Hel` then later `lo"}]}` and parse blows up. Using our fetch+ReadableStream parsing code. Anyone seen this pattern? logs attached.

maria: hmm, is this from EventSource or fetch stream? can you paste the parsing loop?

jamal: fetch w/ response.body.getReader(), TextDecoder, accumulating buffer then splitting on '\n\n' for SSE events. here's simplified version:
```js
const reader = res.body.getReader();
const dec = new TextDecoder();
let buf = '';
while(true){
  const {done, value} = await reader.read();
  if(done) break;
  buf += dec.decode(value, {stream: true});
  const events = buf.split('\n\n');
  buf = events.pop() || '';
  for(const ev of events){
    const lines = ev.split('\n');
    const data = lines.filter(l => l.startsWith('data:')).map(l => l.slice(5)).join('\n');
    JSON.parse(data); // sometimes fails
  }
}
```
Token refresh handler returns 401 and we do a reconnect, but the buffer sometimes contains only half of JSON when connection drops.

kevin: Two issues:
1) Splitting on `\n\n` is brittle if chunk boundaries split within `\n\n` sequence. You should only split on *complete* event delimiter; keeping leftover in buf is right, but ensure you only pop last partial if !buf.endsWith('\n\n').
2) If auth returns 401 mid-stream and you reconnect, there's no guaranteed resume point for in-flight partial JSON events — you need server-side event ids or make each chunk self-contained (NDJSON) so you don't depend on partial assembly.

alex: Also watch TextDecoder behavior for multi-byte UTF-8 split across chunks. Use `dec.decode(value, {stream: true})` (you're already doing that) but make sure you don't call `dec.decode()` without stream flag on last chunk. If you decode with stream: true, the leftover bytes are buffered correctly.

maria: For backpressure in Node, prefer using a TransformStream / async iterator and pause the reader while downstream queue is full. Example pattern:
```js
const reader = res.body.getReader();
while(true){
  const {done, value} = await reader.read();
  if(done) break;
  await writeQueue.push(value); // backpressure
}
```
We use a semaphore with capacity = highWaterMark.

jamal: good tips — regarding reconnecting: is it realistic to ask server to send events as NDJSON (one JSON per data line) instead of arbitrary chunks? would simplify.

kevin: yes, NDJSON is way simpler for clients. If that's not possible, server must include `id:` per SSE event so client can reconnect with Last-Event-ID and server can replay from that id.

jamal: ok I'll open a PR for client: (1) stricter event splitting, (2) UTF-8 safe decode, (3) reconnect logic that drops partial buffer unless last event id is present. Also will add tests simulating split multibyte + 401 mid-stream.

alex: can you add a small harness in streaming-tests/ that emits split chunks and toggles 401 after N bytes? would be great.

jamal: yep, will do. pinging @maria for review when draft is ready :slightly_smiling_face:

deploy-bot: streaming-helpers/frag-safety branch CI passed :white_check_mark:

kevin: also something to watch: some browsers coalesce tiny chunks which changes test timing; make your harness produce a variety of chunk sizes.

maria: noted — thanks all. I'll review the PR and label it backport if needed. :thumbsup:
